---
import ContentDisclaimer from "../../../components/ContentDisclaimer.astro";
import ArticleShare from "../../../components/ArticleShare.astro";
import ArticleDemoCallout from "../../../components/ArticleDemoCallout.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/blog/soap-vs-dap-notes/"]}>
  <main id="main" class="growth-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <a href="/tools/">Resources</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">SOAP or DAP? Work through the format.</span>
      </nav>
      <header class="growth-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">Documentation · By Otto editorial</div>
        <h1>SOAP or DAP? Work through the format.</h1>
        <p>
          We compare how each format organizes the same information, so you can
          choose an approach that fits your practice’s documentation
          requirements.
        </p>
      </header>
      <div class="byline">
        <span>
          By <a href="/authors/otto-editorial/">Otto editorial</a> ·{" "}
          <time datetime="2026-10-16">October 16, 2026</time> · 4 min read
        </span>
      </div>
      <ArticleShare title={pages["/blog/soap-vs-dap-notes/"].title} />
      <div class="format-art" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="180 0 760 390" fill="none">
          <g stroke="#417e86" stroke-width="2">
            <rect x="240" y="70" width="120" height="76" rx="12" />
            <rect x="414" y="70" width="120" height="76" rx="12" />
            <rect x="588" y="70" width="120" height="76" rx="12" />
            <rect x="762" y="70" width="120" height="76" rx="12" />
            <path
              d="M300 164v20q0 12 12 12h150q12 0 12-12v-20M648 164v50m174-50v50"
              opacity=".45"
            />
            <rect x="327" y="242" width="120" height="76" rx="12" />
            <rect x="588" y="242" width="120" height="76" rx="12" />
            <rect x="762" y="242" width="120" height="76" rx="12" />
          </g>
          <path
            d="M264 94h70m-70 20h45m129-20h70m-70 20h45m129-20h70m-70 20h45m129-20h70m-70 20h45M351 266h70m-70 20h45m216-20h70m-70 20h45m129-20h70m-70 20h45"
            stroke="#417e86"
            stroke-width="5"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            opacity=".45"
          />
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="post-layout">
        <aside class="toc">
          <div class="toc-inner">
            <div class="companion-links">
              <h2>Companion resources</h2>
              <a href="/templates/soap-notes/">SOAP note template</a>
              <a href="/templates/dap-notes/">DAP note template</a>
            </div>
            <ArticleDemoCallout />
          </div>
        </aside>
        <article>
          <div class="growth-answer">
            <strong>The practical difference</strong>
            <p>
              SOAP separates Subjective and Objective information. DAP brings
              those observations and reports together under Data. Both include
              an Assessment and Plan.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="growth-section prose">
            <h2>We start with the information you need to document.</h2>
            <p>
              A format gives the note a structure. Your clinical setting,
              documentation policy, payer requirements, and the encounter
              determine what the record needs to contain. We’d choose the
              structure that helps you make those distinctions consistently.
            </p>
            <div class="table-scroll">
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Information</th>
                    <th>SOAP</th>
                    <th>DAP</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Client-reported experience</td>
                    <td>Subjective</td>
                    <td>Data</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Observations, measures, interventions, and response</td>
                    <td>
                      Objective or the appropriate section under your
                      documentation policy
                    </td>
                    <td>Data</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Clinical interpretation and progress</td>
                    <td>Assessment</td>
                    <td>Assessment</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Agreed next steps</td>
                    <td>Plan</td>
                    <td>Plan</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <h2>Try the same fictional session in both.</h2>
            <p>
              Our examples follow a fictional client practicing a response to
              work messages. In SOAP, we separate what the client reports from
              what happens in the session. In DAP, those details share a Data
              section. The assessment still needs the clinician’s reasoning in
              either format.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="resource-cards">
            <a class="resource-card" href="/templates/soap-notes/">
              <span class="tag">Four-part format</span>
              <h3>SOAP note template</h3>
              <p>
                Separate subjective and objective information, then document
                your assessment and plan.
              </p>
              <span class="text-link">Explore SOAP </span>
            </a>
            <a class="resource-card" href="/templates/dap-notes/">
              <span class="tag">Three-part format</span>
              <h3>DAP note template</h3>
              <p>Organize the session into Data, Assessment, and Plan.</p>
              <span class="text-link">Explore DAP </span>
            </a>
          </div>
          <div class="growth-section prose">
            <h2>Three questions we would use to choose</h2>
            <ol>
              <li>
                Does the format meet the documentation requirements that apply
                to your work?
              </li>
              <li>
                Can another authorized clinician follow the encounter and the
                next steps?
              </li>
              <li>
                Can you distinguish the client’s account, observed information,
                and your assessment without duplicating whole paragraphs?
              </li>
            </ol>
            <p>
              There is no universal winning format. Test a fictional encounter
              in each, review it with the appropriate clinical owner, and use
              the structure your practice approves.
            </p>
            <h2>How this relates to Otto</h2>
            <p>
              Otto’s public workflow describes SOAP and DAP drafts from session
              audio, followed by clinician review and signature. A draft still
              needs checking against the encounter. Our template examples are
              editorial illustrations; they are not generated by the Otto
              product.
            </p>
            <a class="button" href="/demo/#watch">
              Watch Otto’s workflow
            </a>
          </div>
          <ContentDisclaimer kind="article" />
          <div class="sources">
            <h2>Sources and review</h2>
            <p>
              Sources checked October 16, 2026. Confirm current product terms
              before choosing software.
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <a href="https://www.simplepractice.com/resource/soap-note-examples/">
                  SOAP note format
                </a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="https://www.mentalyc.com/blog/dap-notes">
                  DAP note format
                </a>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
    <section class="cta-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="cta">
          <div>
            <h2>Make more room for the work you love.</h2>
            <p>
              See how Otto brings notes, scheduling, telehealth, and payments
              into your practice day.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
            Join the waitlist <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  h1,
  h2 {
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  p {
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .growth-page > .wrap,
  .cta-section .wrap {
    max-width: 1200px;
    padding: 0 clamp(20px, 4vw, 56px);
  }
  .growth-page {
    padding-top: 40px;
  }
  .breadcrumbs {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 20px;
  }
  .breadcrumbs a {
    color: var(--deep-teal);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .growth-hero {
    max-width: none;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 1.44px;
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
  }
  .eyebrow::before {
    display: none;
  }
  .growth-hero h1 {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 4.4vw, 60px);
    line-height: 1.04;
    font-weight: 300;
    letter-spacing: -1.4px;
  }
  .growth-hero > p {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 30px;
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
  }
  .byline {
    justify-content: flex-start;
    min-height: 0;
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    padding: 16px 0 8px;
    border-block: 1px solid #e1ded8;
    border-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 20px;
  }
  .byline a {
    color: var(--deep-teal);
  }
  .format-art {
    margin-top: 28px;
    height: 390px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 20px;
    background: #f0eee8;
  }
  .format-art svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }
  .post-layout {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 40px 56px;
    max-width: none;
    margin: 40px 0 64px;
  }
  .toc {
    flex: 1 1 260px;
    max-width: 300px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
  }
  .toc-inner {
    position: static;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .companion-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 20px;
    border: 1px solid #e1ded8;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--white);
  }
  .toc h2 {
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  .companion-links > a {
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    color: var(--deep-teal);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .post-layout > article {
    flex: 999 1 560px;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 780px;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 29px;
  }
  .growth-answer {
    margin: 0 0 40px;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: rgba(65, 126, 134, 0.22);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .growth-answer > strong {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 29px;
    letter-spacing: 1.2px;
  }
  .growth-answer p {
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 30px;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .growth-section.prose {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 29px;
  }
  .growth-section.prose h2 {
    margin: 40px 0 12px;
    font-size: 30px;
    line-height: 36px;
    font-weight: 300;
    letter-spacing: -0.6px;
  }
  .growth-section.prose > h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .growth-section.prose p {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .table-scroll {
    margin: 8px 0 24px;
    border: 1px solid #e1ded8;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--white);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .prose table {
    overflow-wrap: normal;
    width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
  }
  .prose th,
  .prose td {
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e1ded8;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .prose th {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .prose tbody tr:last-child td {
    border: 0;
  }
  .table-scroll + h2 {
    margin-top: 16px !important;
  }
  .growth-page .post-layout .resource-cards {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
    margin: 8px 0 40px;
  }
  .growth-page .post-layout .resource-card {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 20px 22px;
    border: 1px solid #e1ded8;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--white);
  }
  .resource-card:hover {
    transform: none;
    box-shadow: none;
  }
  .resource-card .tag {
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 16px;
    letter-spacing: 1.44px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
  }
  .growth-page .post-layout .resource-card h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 28px;
    font-weight: 300;
    letter-spacing: -0.3px;
  }
  .resource-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 29px;
  }
  .resource-card .text-link {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 29px;
  }
  .prose ol {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  .prose li {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .prose .button {
    min-height: 44px;
    color: var(--white);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 16px;
  }
  .growth-page .sources {
    margin: 32px 0 0;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    border: 1px solid #e1ded8;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--white);
  }
  .sources h2 {
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 29px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  .sources p {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
  }
  .sources ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 26px;
  }
  .sources a {
    color: var(--deep-teal);
  }
  .toc :global(.article-demo-callout) {
    display: block;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid #e1ded8;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--white);
  }
  .toc :global(.article-demo-art) {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 10px;
    height: 150px;
    min-height: 0;
    padding: 0;
    background: var(--growth-2);
  }
  .toc :global(.article-demo-art::before) {
    display: none;
  }
  .toc :global(.article-demo-art img) {
    width: 64px;
    height: auto;
    margin: 0;
    filter: brightness(0) invert(1);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .toc :global(.demo-play-mark) {
    position: static;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    margin: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: var(--attention);
    color: var(--white);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .toc :global(.demo-art-caption) {
    position: static;
    display: block;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--white);
  }
  .toc :global(.article-demo-copy) {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }
  .toc :global(.article-demo-copy .tag) {
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 1.44px;
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
  }
  .toc :global(.article-demo-copy h3) {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 28px;
    font-weight: 300;
    letter-spacing: -0.3px;
  }
  .toc :global(.article-demo-copy p) {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 22px;
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
  }
  .toc :global(.article-demo-copy .button) {
    min-height: 40px;
    padding: 0 24px;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 22px;
  }
  .toc :global(.demo-duration) {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 20px;
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
  }
  .cta-section {
    padding: 64px 0;
    background: var(--white);
  }
  .cta {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 24px 48px;
    padding: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px) clamp(28px, 4vw, 56px);
  }
  .cta > div {
    flex: 1 1 520px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .cta h2 {
    max-width: none;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 3vw, 42px);
    line-height: 1.08;
    font-weight: 300;
    letter-spacing: -0.8px;
  }
  .cta p {
    max-width: none;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 28px;
  }
  .cta .button {
    border: 1px solid var(--white);
  }
  @media (max-width: 950px) {
    .post-layout {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
    }
    .toc {
      order: 1;
      flex: auto;
      max-width: none;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
    .post-layout > article {
      flex: auto;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: none;
    }
    .toc { width: 100%; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .growth-hero h1 {
      font-size: 40px;
    }
    .format-art {
      height: 300px;
    }
    .format-art svg {
      width: 100%;
    }
    .growth-page .post-layout .resource-cards {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .cta {
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
    .cta > div {
      flex-basis: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
